5. Compute Shared Secret (Hybrid / Encap)
Hybrid: Compute ECDH shared secret (Z_ecdh) AND Encapsulate PQC shared secret (Z_kem). Derive final Z = SHA256(Z_ecdh || Z_kem). Pure: Encapsulate only.
// SoftHSMv3 WASM: Profile C Hybrid — ML-KEM Encap + ECDH + Z Combination // Step A: ML-KEM-768 Encapsulation → Z_kem + KEM ciphertext // → C_EncapsulateKey(CKM_ML_KEM) const { ciphertextBytes, secretHandle } = hsm_pqcEncap(M, hSession, hnPubHandle, 'ML-KEM-768') const zKemBytes = hsm_extractKeyValue(M, hSession, secretHandle) // Step B (hybrid only): X25519 ECDH(ephPriv, hnEccPub) → Z_ecdh // PKCS#11 v3.2: CKM_ECDH1_DERIVE (0x1050) is used; SoftHSMv3 routes to // Montgomery DH because the private key has CKA_KEY_TYPE=CKK_EC_MONTGOMERY. // → C_DeriveKey(CKM_ECDH1_DERIVE) — X25519 path selected by key type const hnEccPubBytes = hsm_extractECPoint(M, hSession, hnEccPubHandle) const zEcdhHandle = hsm_ecdhDerive(M, hSession, ephPrivHandle, hnEccPubBytes) const zEcdhBytes = hsm_extractKeyValue(M, hSession, zEcdhHandle) // Step C: Z = SHA256(Z_ecdh || Z_kem) — this project's hybrid combiner const Z = hsm_digest(M, hSession, concat(zEcdhBytes, zKemBytes), CKM_SHA256)
6. Derive Keys (KDF w/ SHA3)
# ANSI X9.63 KDF with SHA3-256, 2 iterations (this project's choice) # Hybrid: Z = SHA256(Z_ecdh ‖ Z_kem), SharedInfo = raw X25519 eph pub key (32 bytes) # Pure PQC: Z = Z_kem, SharedInfo = empty block1 = SHA3_256(Z || 0x00000001 || SharedInfo) # 32 bytes → K_enc (AES-256) block2 = SHA3_256(Z || 0x00000002 || SharedInfo) # 32 bytes → K_mac (HMAC-SHA3-256) enc_key = block1 # 256-bit AES-256 key (full block1) mac_key = block2 # 256-bit HMAC-SHA3-256 key (full block2)
[USIM] Deriving Keys w/ SHA3... [USIM] K_enc: 256-bit AES Key [USIM] K_mac: 256-bit HMAC Key
ANSI X9.63 KDF + FIPS 203 — no 3GPP profile
TS 33.501 Annex C defines Profiles A and B only. "Profile C" is a research proposal (Khan, Purification & Chang, Information 2025, 16, 617); this KDF and the hybrid combiner were added here, not taken from a spec. No test vectors exist for any of it. Execute the step to see live computed values.
Hybrid: SHA256(Z_ecdh ‖ Z_kem) | Pure: Z_kem directly
32-byte output. Full block1 becomes K_enc (AES-256). SHA3-256 chosen for added resilience (ATIS: SHA-256 is secure against quantum attacks for now).
32-byte output. Full block2 becomes K_mac (HMAC-SHA3-256).
Hybrid: raw X25519 eph pub key (32 bytes) | Pure PQC: empty (0 bytes)
Pure PQC mode omits SharedInfo because there is no ECDH ephemeral key. Nothing specifies this either way — it follows from there being no ephemeral EC key to bind in.
block2 (32 bytes) → HMAC-SHA3-256, truncated to 8 bytes on-air
Profile C uses HMAC-SHA3-256 instead of HMAC-SHA-256. Only the first 8 bytes of the tag are kept in the PSC1 sample envelope.
This is the Encryption Point (AES-256-CTR). AES-CTR is length-preserving — the ciphertext has the same byte length as the plaintext MSIN, keeping the SUCI compact over the air interface.
