10. Assemble PSC1 Envelope (Profile C)
Concatenate the header, the ephemeral key (hybrid), the KEM ciphertext, the encrypted MSIN and the 8-byte MAC into one byte string. These bytes are all the network side receives. PSC1 is a project sample format, not a standard, and it does not use an assigned 3GPP protection-scheme identifier.
const psc1 = concat(header, ephPub /* hybrid only */, kemCt, encMSIN, macTag);
[USIM] PSC1 envelope: 1,116 bytes (pure) / 1,148 bytes (hybrid)
11. Network SIDF: Decrypt PSC1 Envelope (Decryption Point)
For Profile C, the SIDF parses the received PSC1 bytes, decapsulates the ML-KEM ciphertext with its own private key, derives the ECDH secret from the transmitted ephemeral key (hybrid), and verifies the MAC over the whole message before decrypting. It uses nothing the sender derived. Authenticate-then-decrypt follows the ECIES pattern TS 33.501 Annex C uses for Profiles A and B: the MAC MUST pass before decryption begins.
// SoftHSMv3 WASM: Profile C SIDF — Hybrid Deconcealment // 0. Parse ONLY the received PSC1 bytes: header, [ephPub], kemCiphertext, encMsin, tag const { ephPub, kemCiphertext, encMsin, tag, macInput } = parsePsc1(receivedBytes) // 1. ML-KEM-768 Decapsulation → Z_kem // → C_DecapsulateKey(CKM_ML_KEM) const zKemHandle = hsm_pqcDecap(M, hSession, hnPrivHandle, kemCiphertext, 'ML-KEM-768') const zKemBytes = hsm_extractKeyValue(M, hSession, zKemHandle) // 2. Hybrid only: X25519 ECDH(hn_ecc_priv, eph_pub) → Z_ecdh, then combine // PKCS#11 v3.2: CKM_ECDH1_DERIVE (0x1050) is used for both X25519 and P-256. // SoftHSMv3 routes to Montgomery DH because hnEccPrivHandle has CKA_KEY_TYPE=CKK_EC_MONTGOMERY. // → C_DeriveKey(CKM_ECDH1_DERIVE) — X25519 path selected by key type // ephPub comes from the received bytes, not from a sender handle const zEcdhHandle = hsm_ecdhDerive(M, hSession, hnEccPrivHandle, ephPub) const zEcdhBytes = hsm_extractKeyValue(M, hSession, zEcdhHandle) const Z = hsm_digest(M, hSession, concat(zEcdhBytes, zKemBytes), CKM_SHA256) // 3. ANSI X9.63-KDF (SHA3-256) const kEnc = hsm_digest(M, hSession, concat(Z, 0x00000001, sharedInfo), CKM_SHA3_256) const kMac = hsm_digest(M, hSession, concat(Z, 0x00000002, sharedInfo), CKM_SHA3_256) // 4. Authenticate-then-decrypt: verify MAC BEFORE decryption // The MAC covers every byte before the tag, not just the MSIN ciphertext const macBytes = hsm_hmac(M, hSession, kMacHandle, macInput, CKM_SHA3_256_HMAC) if (!timingSafeEqual(macBytes.slice(0, 8), tag)) throw new Error('MAC mismatch — envelope rejected by SIDF') // 5. Decrypt MSIN only after MAC passes (AES-256-CTR, zero IV) const msinBcd = hsm_aesDecrypt(M, hSession, kEncHandle, encMsin, zeroIv, 'ctr') const supi = mcc + mnc + bcdDecode(msinBcd)
